> Status: `todo` / `in-progress` / `in-review` / `done` / `blocked`. Lifecycle: `todo → in-progress → in-review → done`. `ccf-implementer` marks `in-review` when code+test are complete; only `/ccf:updatespec` writes `done` after `/ccf:check` + `/code-review` pass.
> Write the status as a **bare word** — no `**bold**` around it. Emphasis carries no information and the status is matched as a whole word.
> Per-task detail in `task-NNN-*.md`.

> **Keep this file to the CURRENT iteration.** When every task of an iteration is `done`, `/ccf:updatespec` moves its sections verbatim into `.claude/plan/ARCHIVE.md` and `git mv`s its `task-NNN-*.md` files into `.claude/plan/archive/`. Two reasons, pulling in opposite directions: a closed row left here is counted as live work by the session-start and Stop hooks, while DELETING the history would strip `ccf-spec-checker`'s premortem of the real past failures it anchors to. So archive, never delete.
